# pr-review Layer 2 (repo memory: mined learnings, finding history, false-positive log)
# must survive a fresh clone. Git cannot re-include a path whose parent dir is excluded,
# so the negation walks down and re-ignores siblings at each level. Everything else under
# .claude/ — settings.local.json, projects/ auto-memory, other skills — stays local-only.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/pr-review/
!.claude/skills/triage-pr-comments/
# Keep OS cruft and the miner's scratch cache out even where the negations re-include a
# directory. `.mine-cache/` is unanchored so it applies on every agent surface below.
.DS_Store
.mine-cache/
.claude-cache/captures/
.claude-cache/investigations/

# The same skills mirrored to the Codex and .agents surfaces (`sync-skills` keeps the three
# in step). Same walk-down, for the same reason: a bare `!.codex/skills/` cannot re-include
# anything, because `.codex/` above already excluded the parent and git will not descend into
# an excluded directory. Unlike `.claude/` these track every skill, not just the two review
# ones — the mirrors exist to give a fresh clone the full bundle on those surfaces.
!.codex/
.codex/*
!.codex/skills/
!.agents/
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
